ng with me, search all these places. Great men, of your calibre, do remain unagitated even in the midst of difficulties like to mountains never shaken by the velocity of the wind.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-3-67-5"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"3063006","sanskritFile":"Ram03.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"1d2beef1d1b29dbe93095bc01a993fab1914fdbb4afde67167bc60f724fe8e6e","compact":"d7587704855e33a8d935cb4e1dd1619249d991c03b0571d449c9f831252cff63","nasal":"74ac227ec0e64c36f6b635e980531f4d55e5be749c4f502fa9a4d43f649f00a9"}},{"id":"VRCE-3-63-7","kanda":3,"kandaId":"aranya","sarga":63,"verse":7,"english":"Many are the abodes here belonging to the Kinnaras and Gandharvas. Do you, along with me, search all these places. Great men, of your calibre, do remain unagitated even in the midst of difficulties like to mountains never shaken by the velocity of the wind.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.515,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-3-67-5"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"3063007","sanskritFile":"Ram03.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"204ffa39a95a9614b443a2fdc6e622db1971406b361d81e997b1b6b53a22b9d5","compact":"c1e25590dc0c323bd00725f2f2eecb4c8d29a0f94a1dd4bc85f5bf70fcafdd40","nasal":"215c1359fc471c1139a946ee19e5223a0d50c14a40eafeb705e1c7a165b899fd"}},{"id":"VRCE-3-63-8","kanda":3,"kandaId":"aranya","sarga":63,"verse":8,"english":"Many are the abodes here belonging to the Kinnaras and Gandharvas. Do you, along with me, search all these places. Great men, of your calibre, do remain unagitated even in the midst of difficulties like to mountains never shaken by the velocity of the wind. Hearing these words, Rāma, enraged, fixing sharp and terrible arrows to his bow, began to range the forest with Lakşmaņa.","alignment":{"type":"split","confidence":0.46,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-3-67-5","DUTT-3-67-6"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"3063008","sanskritFile":"Ram03.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"2656624cd1b6fb1b2d10bae541a453533d2a135d7ed7080e0d69c140e5b5c37b","compact":"b1134d2ffaf7006f5f7007362f9e5d438197ca61837a69db6c3fea0b930cc1c5","nasal":"12563b95f0316c4b3a105ceb3cc99b7573abfabf2bdf7fe9247cbeb8c4680ce1"}},{"id":"VRCE-3-63-9","kanda":3,"kandaId":"aranya","sarga":63,"verse":9,"english":"Hearing these words, Rāma, enraged, fixing sharp and terrible arrows to his bow, began to range the forest with Lakşmaņa. Thereupon he beheld, fallen on ground, having his person bathed in blood, the king of birds-Jatayu, resembling a mountain peak, and spoke to Lakşmaņa.","alignment":{"type":"split","confidence":0.468,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-3-67-6","DUTT-3-67-7"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"3063009","sanskritFile":"Ram03.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"c38bfa99e60e5ac17fb55f78ff308b3be5467b1b63e868e56a60b3b23ed8d8fc","compact":"6e588d7a4400147051f99cc3179fec8018a7740cdd3bb1879f9038ff0933bf90","nasal":"6e588d7a4400147051f99cc3179fec8018a7740cdd3bb1879f9038ff0933bf90"}},{"id":"VRCE-3-63-10","kanda":3,"kandaId":"aranya","sarga":63,"verse":10,"english":"Thereupon he beheld, fallen on ground, having his person bathed in blood, the king of birds-Jatayu, resembling a mountain peak, and spoke to Lakşmaņa.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.596,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-3-67-7"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"3063010","sanskritFile":"Ram03.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"d680a9106dde932ef788afb7ebf76bfeafe08991ed0f4daae7f4d54f444ae48c","compact":"d38ae470ae704a224083e8c33cfb890b362ce6b84fc8ba1ae014afc8c5b9d094","nasal":"d3423d87ce3fd58a6ea87222