N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"54360a195aa60d2ab0c01b3b75be01195eea96a767e8a76f3af070dfdf803c5f","compact":"7b50cff065edf87415c3ab51eb5971592d685fd255f3dbef8eb367e7401e8df6","nasal":"7b50cff065edf87415c3ab51eb5971592d685fd255f3dbef8eb367e7401e8df6"}},{"id":"VRCE-3-63-14","kanda":3,"kandaId":"aranya","sarga":63,"verse":14,"english":"O you of long life, that goddess, whom you have been searching in this vast forest like to Os adhi, and my life have been carried away by Rāvana.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.873,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-3-67-12"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"3063014","sanskritFile":"Ram03.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"ca79b14e8b42b9e8014ba9fb48eaf760888467d200b0a470cd1a304cef806e32","compact":"6efdceccb5a9eb65b153898332d2af85a0cdc4a051ba181018d339bac87c72a1","nasal":"28caf27d4270b4d777afb1036f11fb29289c505b3be19f83eaf9feda3f1377cf"}},{"id":"VRCE-3-63-15","kanda":3,"kandaId":"aranya","sarga":63,"verse":15,"english":"I saw her, O Rāghava, carried away stealthily by the powerful Rāvaņa, in your absence as well as that of Lakşmaņa.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-3-67-13"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"3063015","sanskritFile":"Ram03.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"21c22ced51b4efb1f8f4cf9c751fc5540772f2f6fec039c3889178deab6136d0","compact":"f4c43a493e26a529c69e3038d8be9631fb899d62aba868d5a2b0c8a95d7eb685","nasal":"f4c43a493e26a529c69e3038d8be9631fb899d62aba868d5a2b0c8a95d7eb685"}},{"id":"VRCE-3-63-16","kanda":3,"kandaId":"aranya","sarga":63,"verse":16,"english":"Myself nearing Sītā, for her rescue, O Lord, Rāvaņa was thrown down on earth by me in conflict having his car and umbrella shattered.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.66,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-3-67-14"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"3063016","sanskritFile":"Ram03.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"80e2fb2e0ccc93dd3f80e9bbc6c1f63b485cbf947a9e91f637ef9187a85f1e38","compact":"bb753b0d88eff95d8cf6ddbc94d097c71ce7330014409e32b67130776a988438","nasal":"f9d4caeac7e27a768e914933da1948d6515af2418512fb78afc33762af6b2f4a"}},{"id":"VRCE-3-63-17","kanda":3,"kandaId":"aranya","sarga":63,"verse":17,"english":"This is his snapped bow and these are his broken shafts. And this is his war-car, O Rāma shattered in fight.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.66,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-3-67-15"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"3063017","sanskritFile":"Ram03.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"434e7beae7fab53f4d4a9032e3beb92c6475e1e5c46caf52881761469d1b04f6","compact":"2d37cd1ed35d898f17b21c2d874f7a3572ff732cb0d85aa036aa819f3101ef1c","nasal":"2d37cd1ed35d898f17b21c2d874f7a3572ff732cb0d85aa036aa819f3101ef1c"}},{"id":"VRCE-3-63-18","kanda":3,"kandaId":"aranya","sarga":63,"verse":18,"english":"This is his charioteer lying on earth being killed by the velocity of my wings. Having sundered my wings with his dagger, who had been exhausted, Rāvana taking Sītā, rose high up in the welkin. It behove you not to kill me who had been wounded before by the Rākşasa.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.657,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-3-67-16"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"3063018","sanskritFile":"Ram03.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"73c71153591304047e154e9881b89437c3819fddd8fb50a36b62f1366d94c413","compact":"2e5a6ec365f051a96919c57aa61fac868b2091d9ff0667ac4f1151908334ab80","nasal":"1648ce90b73f72fd9bea9f998148fafb77f3adca4187b784a79b3f407e38c582"}},{"id":"VRCE-3-63-19","kanda":3,"kandaId":"aranya","sarga":63,"verse":19,"english":"Hearing from him pleasant words relating to Sītā, Rāma, leaving aside, instantly, his mighty bow, embraced him, and rolling on earth having lost self-control through grief, began to lament with Lakşmaņa. Though highly composed by nature, he was overwhelmed with doubled grief.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.894,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-3-67-17"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"3063019","sanskritFile":"Ram03.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"d47912c7caf70a143ed60440d73906eb20abdd7e4cb667e2e7ce33f353cdcd22","compact":"13a3d72077f151a4ea662e772633ebae4720d5909452700490864b8c93c08c8f","nasal":"13a3d72077f151a4ea662e772633ebae4720d5909452700490864b8c93c08c8f"}},{"id":"VRCE-3-63-20","kanda":3,"kandaId":"aranya","sarga":63,"verse":20,"english":"And beholding Jațāyu, sigh again and again and breathing with difficulty in a helpless plight, Rāma, highly aggrieved, spoke to Lakşmaņa.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.548,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-3-67-18"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"3063020","sanskritFile":"Ram03.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"e719da0154a783119979b2cb3eaa86cd35fcb53edc38c7c04feaefb95248c2ec","compact":"8e4b17525cb2ad941eabfa6f14fb9d50cb666622dbfbbf149b3f378d1dd0b86d","nasal":"5bef1b2440380bdb5bd56a3aaed3efad0d2b8474f6fafa937ee8c40a0c3b4c64"}},{"id":"VRCE-3-63-21","kanda":3,"kandaId":"aranya","sarga":63,"verse":21,"english":"I have lost my kingdom and have been living in this forest. My Sītā has been carried away and this bird has been killed (on my account). This misfortune of mine can burn even the very fire.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.448,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-3-67-19"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"3063021","sanskritFile":"Ram03.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"592f88d38f66404af75ccbaa8c27841754bfbb654bd556f43b4df6dc6cadb248","compact":"9a7e9bd184392a739fb4f89e8af0b19585c23ef0d1a0f9ac966b1665b959628f","nasal":"9a7e9bd184392a739fb4f89e8af0b19585c23ef0d1a0f9ac966b1665b959628f"}},{"id":"VRCE-3-63-22","kanda":3,"kandaId":"aranya","sarga":63,"verse":22,"english":"If for assuaging my grief I do enter the mighty ocean, verily shall that misfortune dry up even that lord of rivers.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.969,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-3-67-20"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"3063022","sanskritFile":"Ram03.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"280ee9ca2117e3b3809c4c5806f5ebd25d18f43245edb03c52dfa83267843022","compact":"a5acbaf15d045e6bd071e656e8aa0ac4ece967f8745d6a5a4c158200ecf59520","nasal":"a5acbaf15d045e6bd071e656e8aa0ac4ece967f8745d6a5a4c158200ecf59520"}},{"id":"VRCE-3-63-23","kanda":3,"kandaId":"aranya","sarga":63,"verse":23,"english":"There is none so unfortunate as I, throughout this earth, mobile or immobile, and it is for this bad luck that I have confronted this mighty disaster.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-3-67-21"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"3063023","sanskritFile":"Ram03.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"24aa43e1e7df2b793b0c6a470668328ff42a6b1805421a6ce20eb185cb0d6003","compact":"d30e506af3be787ecee8c1d83f3aaf3c36cc2ed588fcf0f63c36ec3a8d3295d2","nasal":"d30e506af3be787ecee8c1d83f3aaf3c36cc2ed588fcf0f63c36ec3a8d3295d2"}},{"id":"VRCE-3-63-24","kanda":3,"kandaId":"aranya","sarga":63,"verse":24,"english":"This mighty king of vultures is our father's friend and he Leith on earth, killed through the evil turn of my fortune.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.621,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-3-67-22"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"3063024","sanskritFile":"Ram03.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"f85fa1437d5c33fd0a457860dc8a1161867ce346326028b8a8565c05a369d4a7","compact":"d6406774778a87c8dbb87d826f29a83ecbbe2db6fe513b6fb822920165ce05a2","nasal":"d6406774778a87c8dbb87d826f29a83ecbbe2db6fe513b6fb822920165ce05a2"}},{"id":"VRCE-3-63-25","kanda":3,"kandaId":"aranya","sarga":63,"verse":25,"english":"Uttering these and various other words, Rāghava, along with Lakşmaņa touched his body manifesting his paternal affection.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-3-67-23"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"3063025","sanskritFile":"Ram03.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"8241e797c7ccf111305654300ec109f234f134d29b45f46da9410ec4ee8fcf61","compact":"450865e937dedfcaf8297e50f85e9b31ab135b084a5f54d34da6141b1b3b1b8f","nasal":"450865e937dedfcaf8297e50f85e9b31ab135b084a5f54d34da6141b1b3b1b8f"}},{"id":"VRCE-3-63-26","kanda":3,"kandaId":"aranya","sarga":63,"verse":26,"english":"Embracing the king of vultures, bathed in blood, having its wings cut off, Rāghava, fell on the ground, exclaiming where has Maithili gone like to my life?","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.627,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-3-67-24"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"3063026","sanskritFile":"Ram03.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"e88e27b7b155cadbda15641b5fd6c59fa177fa45c825a616473af85e5b5f6ea1","compact":"512afe9272c98722d0cea8b6e9f51599d62db49b56d8ed71f9f2f5a6a4fcf2c3","nasal":"512afe9272c98722d0cea8b6e9f51599d62db49b56d8ed71f9f2f5a6a4fcf2c3"}}]
